# PROJECT AR: MASTER CURSOR RULES & ENGINE SPECIFICATION

You are the Lead Developer for "Project AR", an interactive 3D WebAR Birthday Quest application built with React, Vite, Three.js/Canvas 2D, and WebAudio API.

## PROJECT ARCHITECTURE
- Framework: React (Vite)
- Background Engine: src/components/EnchantedCanvas.jsx (Interactive Lumos 3D Stardust & Golden Snitch spawner)
- Audio Engine: src/utils/audioEngine.js (Centralized WebAudio controller)
- Screen Progression: State machine in src/App.jsx (gateway -> prank -> map -> vault)

## AUDIO ASSET MATRIX (public/audio/)
- Background Music: bgm_intro.mp3, bgm_act1.mp3, bgm_act2.mp3, bgm_act3.mp3
- Sound Effects: sfx_wand_swish.mp3, sfx_spell_quest.mp3, sfx_revelio_bell.mp3, sfx_tile_clack.mp3, sfx_vault_alohomora.mp3, sfx_crystal_touch.mp3, sfx_snitch_wings.mp3, sfx_potion_bubble.mp3, sfx_parchment_rustle.mp3
- Gokul-Mage Voice Clips: voice_tap_yay.mp3, voice_no_nice_try.mp3, voice_kiss_giggle.mp3, voice_idle_hmm.mp3

## CODING RULES
1. ALWAYS import and use audioEngine from ../utils/audioEngine for sound interactions.
2. Use inline styles or modular CSS for components. Maintain dark velvet wizarding theme (#0F0A1C background, #D4AF37 gold accents, #F4E8C1 text).
3. Ensure absolute syntactic cleanliness in React JSX (multi-line, proper closing tags, zero unescaped characters).
4. Keep screens cleanly modular in src/components/.
